data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":107,"item_id":"rs_082f5798d61bd13b016acbadca7ad48197a0c28b66377a9961","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Evaluating date handling**\n\nI’m looking into potential UTF-8 corruption issues with readForm chunks, specifically making sure that the regex for validDueDate works correctly. I need to check if the regex allows for a newline at the end of a valid date format. It seems that having a dollar sign before a final newline could let through an invalid date when I split up the input. I need to ensure strict formatting to disallow newlines and set the length to 10 for validation. Sounds like I’ve got some testing to do!"}}

